  "conclusion": "Holding n and the class counts fixed and varying only d: the WITHIN-PROTOCOL selection optimism (max minus mean over the same splits) does not grow with d in any arm (in-fold -0.0001, leaky-grid +0.0036, leaky-fixed-k +0.0067 AUC per decade of d). Where d does act is on the LEVEL of a leakage-contaminated maximum when the number of selected features is held fixed while the pool grows: the shopped maximum moves +0.0157 AUC/decade under fixed-k full-data selection versus -0.0025 with selection kept in-fold, while honest discrimination itself moves +0.0023. This is the configuration used in results/rd_dose_response.csv, which is why that file shows d correlating with its protocol-crossing gap while the selection optimism modelled in this paper does not."
